INT. GOLDEN MIC KARAOKE - PRIVATE BOOTH - NIGHT

Velvet seats. Disco lights. A screen scrolling lyrics. Five people crowd a booth built for four.

NOLA FINCH, 30s, sequins. ARTHUR BELL, 30s, a sensible sweater. SIMONE RAYE, 30s, bridesmaid in a silver dress. HUGO MARTEL, 40s, shirt open at the collar. KIRA BELL, 20s, Arthur's sister, gripping the mic.

KIRA
(into the mic, off-key)
...and I will always love you...

She finishes. They clap. Nola leans toward Arthur. He leans toward her. She tucks her hair behind her ear. He looks away. She looks at Simone. Simone smiles and looks at Hugo. He raises his glass.

NOLA
Arthur, that was a lovely toast earlier.

ARTHUR
Thank you.

NOLA
You said you've never been happier than tonight.

ARTHUR
I meant it.

NOLA
Me too.

SIMONE
Aw.

HUGO
Cheers.

KIRA
Nola. Arthur. Would you two go up and sing the last one?

NOLA
Oh, we couldn't.

ARTHUR
We really couldn't.

KIRA
You have to. It's tradition.

HUGO
Nola, there is something I need to say first.

NOLA
Hugo?

HUGO
Arthur is not the man you think he is.

ARTHUR
Hugo.

HUGO
Seven years ago he proposed to me.

NOLA
What?

SIMONE
He did?

HUGO
In this same booth.

Nobody breathes. The lyrics keep scrolling.
